Summary of the task and process - Objective: Identify every men’s T20I Player/Man of the Match (before 2023) for whom, in the same match, both teams scored more than 100, he took at least 3 wickets and conceded at least 9 runs; and whose personal details satisfy DOB between 1980–1999 (inclusive) and Test debut between 2010–2019 (inclusive). Then present all plausible candidates with evidence, reasoning, and uncertainties. - Plan executed: 1) Use an internet-enabled research agent to build a comprehensive candidate list from authoritative sources (primarily ESPNcricinfo), filtering to men’s T20Is pre-2023 where the POTM bowler had ≥3 wickets and ≥9 runs conceded, and both teams posted ≥101. 2) Verify player DOB and Test-debut windows on ESPNcricinfo profiles. 3) Compile deduplicated candidates with match details, links, and concise quotations demonstrating the criteria. Flag any data-access issues or edge cases. Working history (high-level) - A single web-research subtask was executed to search ESPNcricinfo match pages and player profiles, supplemented by corroborating sources (e.g., ICC or Wikipedia series pages) when ESPN endpoints were intermittently inaccessible in this environment. - The tool returned a structured report listing eight clear candidates with links, match details, and (where possible) direct ESPN quotations proving: match type/date, POTM, bowling figures, and both teams’ totals. - No further tools were used. I then synthesized the candidates into a concise, deduplicated list and highlighted evidence and uncertainties. Findings: deduplicated list of plausible candidate players All players below satisfy: men’s T20I before 2023; POTM with ≥3 wickets and ≥9 runs conceded; both teams ≥101; DOB in 1980–1999; Test debut 2010–2019. 1) Hardik Pandya (India) - Personal: DOB 11-10-1993; Test debut 26-07-2017 vs Sri Lanka. ESPN profile: http://www.espncricinfo.com/ci/content/player/625371.html - Match: England vs India, 1st T20I, 07-07-2022, Southampton. Result: India won by 50 runs. - Evidence (ESPNcricinfo match report): “India 198/8 … England (19.3/20 ov, T:199) 148 … India won by 50 runs” and “Player Of The Match Hardik Pandya … 51 (33) & 4/33” - Link: https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/india-in-england-2022-1276893/england-vs-india-1st-t20i-1276904/match-report 2) Kuldeep Yadav (India) - Personal: DOB 14-12-1994; Test debut 25-03-2017 vs Australia. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/kuldeep-yadav-559235 - Match: England vs India, 1st T20I, 03-07-2018, Manchester. Result: India won by 8 wickets. - Evidence (ESPNcricinfo match report): “England 159/8 … India (18.2/20 ov, T:160) 163/2 … India won by 8 wickets” and “Player Of The Match Kuldeep Yadav … 5/24” - Link: https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/india-tour-of-england-2018-1119528/england-vs-india-1st-t20i-1119543/match-report 3) Bhuvneshwar Kumar (India) - Personal: DOB 05-02-1990; Test debut 22-02-2013 vs Australia. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/ci/content/player/326016.html - Match: South Africa vs India, 1st T20I, 18-02-2018, Johannesburg. Result: India won by 28 runs. - Evidence: India 203/5; South Africa 175/9; POTM Bhuvneshwar Kumar; bowling 5/24 (4-0-24-5). ESPN match page (reference, intermittently inaccessible here): https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/india-tour-of-south-africa-2017-18-1122268/south-africa-vs-india-1st-t20i-1130743; corroborated by ICC/Wikipedia summaries noting his first T20I five-for and match result. - Criteria: Both teams ≥101; wickets ≥3 and runs conceded ≥9; pre-2023 T20I; personal windows met. 4) Lockie Ferguson (New Zealand) - Personal: DOB 13-06-1991; Test debut 12-12-2019 vs Australia. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/lockie-ferguson-493773 - Match: New Zealand vs West Indies, 1st T20I, 27-11-2020, Auckland. Result: New Zealand won by 5 wickets. - Evidence: POTM Lockie Ferguson; 5/21; WI 180/7; NZ 185/5. ESPN match-report link (reference): https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/west-indies-in-nz-2020-21-1233943/new-zealand-vs-west-indies-1st-t20i-1233953/match-report 5) Lungi Ngidi (South Africa) - Personal: DOB 29-03-1996; Test debut 13-01-2018 vs India. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/lungi-ngidi-542023 - Match: South Africa vs England, 1st T20I, 12-02-2020, East London. Result: South Africa won by 1 run. - Evidence: POTM Lungi Ngidi; 3/30; SA 177/8; ENG 176/9. ESPN match-report (reference): https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/england-in-sa-2019-20-1193509/south-africa-vs-england-1st-t20i-1194498/match-report (ICC summary corroborates: “Ngidi defends seven to win from final over …”) 6) Jason Holder (West Indies) - Personal: DOB 05-11-1991; Test debut 26-06-2014 vs New Zealand. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/jason-holder-391485 - Match: West Indies vs England, 5th T20I, 30-01-2022, Bridgetown. Result: West Indies won by 17 runs. - Evidence: POTM Jason Holder; 5/27 (incl. four in four); WI 179/4; ENG 162. ESPN match-report link: https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/england-tour-of-west-indies-2021-22-1256716/west-indies-vs-england-5th-t20i-1256724/match-report 7) Sam Curran (England) - Personal: DOB 03-06-1998; Test debut 01-06-2018 vs Pakistan. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/sam-curran-662973 - Match: England vs Afghanistan, T20 World Cup 2022 (Group 1), 22-10-2022, Perth. Result: England won by 5 wickets. - Evidence: POTM Sam Curran; 5/10; AFG 112; ENG 113/5. ESPN match-report link: https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/icc-men-s-t20-world-cup-2022-129813/england-vs-afghanistan-group-1-12th-match-1298147/match-report 8) Josh Hazlewood (Australia) - Personal: DOB 08-01-1991; Test debut 17-12-2014 vs India. ESPN profile: https://www.espncricinfo.com/cricketers/josh-hazlewood-288284 - Match: Australia vs Sri Lanka, 1st T20I, 11-02-2022, Sydney. Result: Australia won. - Evidence: POTM Josh Hazlewood; 4/12; AUS 149/9; SL 122/8. ESPN match-report link: https://www.espncricinfo.com/series/sri-lanka-in-australia-2021-22-1263066/australia-vs-sri-lanka-1st-t20i-1263072/match-report Concise ESPNcricinfo quotations captured directly - Hardik Pandya, ENG v IND 1st T20I (07-07-2022): - “India 198/8 … England (19.3/20 ov, T:199) 148 … India won by 50 runs” - “Player Of The Match Hardik Pandya … 51 (33) & 4/33” - Kuldeep Yadav, ENG v IND 1st T20I (03-07-2018): - “England 159/8 … India (18.2/20 ov, T:160) 163/2 … India won by 8 wickets” - “Player Of The Match Kuldeep Yadav … 5/24” Edge cases, uncertainties, and completeness - Access limitations: Some ESPNcricinfo pages intermittently returned 403/404 in this environment (e.g., SA v IND 1st T20I on 18 Feb 2018). For these, the ESPN link is still provided and the facts (POTM, bowling figures, team totals) are corroborated via ICC or Wikipedia series pages (which in turn cite ESPN). Where possible, direct ESPN quotations are included above. - All listed matches meet the thresholds strictly: both teams ≥101; bowler took ≥3 wickets and conceded ≥9 runs; men’s T20Is before 2023; and all players meet DOB/Test-debut windows. - Completeness: The eight players above are strong, well-documented cases across major teams. Other less-publicised or Associate-member T20Is may also contain qualifying instances; a full database sweep could add more names if desired. Final answer - The description does not single out a unique individual. Based on the comprehensive web-research report assembled, the plausible candidates that satisfy all conditions are: \boxed{Hardik Pandya, Kuldeep Yadav, Bhuvneshwar Kumar, Lockie Ferguson, Lungi Ngidi, Jason Holder, Sam Curran, Josh Hazlewood}
